WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.652
Checkpoint question.

00:00:01.652 --> 00:00:10.767
What is the Lang Graph equivalent of a Python statement that says: if the score passes the threshold, generate;

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:16.292
otherwise, rewrite? The answer is a conditional edge.

00:00:16.292 --> 00:00:19.422
A vector store handles retrieval.

00:00:19.422 --> 00:00:22.782
The tool decorator exposes a capability.

00:00:22.782 --> 00:00:25.690
Neither one represents the branch itself.

00:00:26.672 --> 00:00:31.704
Conditional edges are how graph topology expresses if and else behavior.

00:00:31.704 --> 00:00:35.346
So the correct answer is: a conditional edge.
